{
  "version": "2.1.0",
  "$schema": "https://docs.oasis-open.org/sarif/sarif/v2.1.0/errata01/os/schemas/sarif-schema-2.1.0.json",
  "runs": [
    {
      "tool": {
        "driver": {
          "name": "grype",
          "version": "0.115.0",
          "informationUri": "https://github.com/anchore/grype",
          "rules": [
            {
              "id": "CVE-2011-3389-libgnutls30",
              "name": "DpkgMatcherExactIndirectMatch",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CVE-2011-3389 low vulnerability for libgnutls30 package"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "The SSL protocol, as used in certain configurations in Microsoft Windows and Microsoft Internet Explorer, Mozilla Firefox, Google Chrome, Opera, and other products, encrypts data by using CBC mode with chained initialization vectors, which allows man-in-the-middle attackers to obtain plaintext HTTP headers via a blockwise chosen-boundary attack (BCBA) on an HTTPS session, in conjunction with JavaScript code that uses (1) the HTML5 WebSocket API, (2) the Java URLConnection API, or (3) the Silverlight WebClient API, aka a \"BEAST\" attack."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://security-tracker.debian.org/tracker/CVE-2011-3389",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2011-3389\nSeverity: low\nPackage: libgnutls30\nVersion: 3.7.9-2+deb12u7\nFix Version: \nType: deb\nLocation: /var/lib/dpkg/status\nData Namespace: debian:distro:debian:12\nLink: [CVE-2011-3389](https://security-tracker.debian.org/tracker/CVE-2011-3389)",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2011-3389**\n| Severity | Package | Version | Fix Version | Type | Location | Data Namespace | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| low  | libgnutls30  | 3.7.9-2+deb12u7  |   | deb  | /var/lib/dpkg/status  | debian:distro:debian:12  | [CVE-2011-3389](https://security-tracker.debian.org/tracker/CVE-2011-3389)  |\n"
              },
              "properties": {
                "purls": [
                  "pkg:deb/debian/libgnutls30@3.7.9-2%2Bdeb12u7?arch=amd64\u0026distro=debian-12\u0026upstream=gnutls28"
                ],
                "security-severity": "4.3"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "CVE-2023-2953-libldap-2.5-0",
              "name": "DpkgMatcherExactIndirectMatch",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CVE-2023-2953 high vulnerability for libldap-2.5-0 package"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "A vulnerability was found in openldap. This security flaw causes a null pointer dereference in ber_memalloc_x() function."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://security-tracker.debian.org/tracker/CVE-2023-2953",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2023-2953\nSeverity: high\nPackage: libldap-2.5-0\nVersion: 2.5.13+dfsg-5\nFix Version: \nType: deb\nLocation: /var/lib/dpkg/status\nData Namespace: debian:distro:debian:12\nLink: [CVE-2023-2953](https://security-tracker.debian.org/tracker/CVE-2023-2953)",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2023-2953**\n| Severity | Package | Version | Fix Version | Type | Location | Data Namespace | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| high  | libldap-2.5-0  | 2.5.13+dfsg-5  |   | deb  | /var/lib/dpkg/status  | debian:distro:debian:12  | [CVE-2023-2953](https://security-tracker.debian.org/tracker/CVE-2023-2953)  |\n"
              },
              "properties": {
                "purls": [
                  "pkg:deb/debian/libldap-2.5-0@2.5.13%2Bdfsg-5?arch=amd64\u0026distro=debian-12\u0026upstream=openldap"
                ],
                "security-severity": "7.5"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-11856-curl",
              "name": "DpkgMatcherExactDirectMatch",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CVE-2026-11856 critical vulnerability for curl package"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "Successfully using libcurl to do a transfer to a specific HTTP origin (`hostA`) with **Digest** authentication and then changing the origin to a different one (`hostB`) for a second transfer, reusing the same handle, makes libcurl wrongly pass on the  `Authorization:` header field meant for `hostA`, to `hostB`."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://security-tracker.debian.org/tracker/CVE-2026-11856",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2026-11856\nSeverity: critical\nPackage: curl\nVersion: 7.88.1-10+deb12u15\nFix Version: \nType: deb\nLocation: /var/lib/dpkg/status\nData Namespace: debian:distro:debian:12\nLink: [CVE-2026-11856](https://security-tracker.debian.org/tracker/CVE-2026-11856)",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2026-11856**\n| Severity | Package | Version | Fix Version | Type | Location | Data Namespace | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| critical  | curl  | 7.88.1-10+deb12u15  |   | deb  | /var/lib/dpkg/status  | debian:distro:debian:12  | [CVE-2026-11856](https://security-tracker.debian.org/tracker/CVE-2026-11856)  |\n"
              },
              "properties": {
                "purls": [
                  "pkg:deb/debian/curl@7.88.1-10%2Bdeb12u15?arch=amd64\u0026distro=debian-12"
                ],
                "security-severity": "9.8"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-11856-libcurl4",
              "name": "DpkgMatcherExactIndirectMatch",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CVE-2026-11856 critical vulnerability for libcurl4 package"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "Successfully using libcurl to do a transfer to a specific HTTP origin (`hostA`) with **Digest** authentication and then changing the origin to a different one (`hostB`) for a second transfer, reusing the same handle, makes libcurl wrongly pass on the  `Authorization:` header field meant for `hostA`, to `hostB`."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://security-tracker.debian.org/tracker/CVE-2026-11856",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2026-11856\nSeverity: critical\nPackage: libcurl4\nVersion: 7.88.1-10+deb12u15\nFix Version: \nType: deb\nLocation: /var/lib/dpkg/status\nData Namespace: debian:distro:debian:12\nLink: [CVE-2026-11856](https://security-tracker.debian.org/tracker/CVE-2026-11856)",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2026-11856**\n| Severity | Package | Version | Fix Version | Type | Location | Data Namespace | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| critical  | libcurl4  | 7.88.1-10+deb12u15  |   | deb  | /var/lib/dpkg/status  | debian:distro:debian:12  | [CVE-2026-11856](https://security-tracker.debian.org/tracker/CVE-2026-11856)  |\n"
              },
              "properties": {
                "purls": [
                  "pkg:deb/debian/libcurl4@7.88.1-10%2Bdeb12u15?arch=amd64\u0026distro=debian-12\u0026upstream=curl"
                ],
                "security-severity": "9.8"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-10536-curl",
              "name": "DpkgMatcherExactDirectMatch",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CVE-2026-10536 critical vulnerability for curl package"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "A use-after-free vulnerability exists in libcurl when an application configures an HTTP/2 stream-dependency tree via `CURLOPT_STREAM_DEPENDS` or `CURLOPT_STREAM_DEPENDS_E`, subsequently invokes `curl_easy_reset()`, and finally terminates the handle with `curl_easy_cleanup()`. During this final cleanup phase, libcurl attempts to access and modify an internal structure that was already freed during the reset operation."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://security-tracker.debian.org/tracker/CVE-2026-10536",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2026-10536\nSeverity: critical\nPackage: curl\nVersion: 7.88.1-10+deb12u15\nFix Version: \nType: deb\nLocation: /var/lib/dpkg/status\nData Namespace: debian:distro:debian:12\nLink: [CVE-2026-10536](https://security-tracker.debian.org/tracker/CVE-2026-10536)",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2026-10536**\n| Severity | Package | Version | Fix Version | Type | Location | Data Namespace | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| critical  | curl  | 7.88.1-10+deb12u15  |   | deb  | /var/lib/dpkg/status  | debian:distro:debian:12  | [CVE-2026-10536](https://security-tracker.debian.org/tracker/CVE-2026-10536)  |\n"
              },
              "properties": {
                "purls": [
                  "pkg:deb/debian/curl@7.88.1-10%2Bdeb12u15?arch=amd64\u0026distro=debian-12"
                ],
                "security-severity": "9.8"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-10536-libcurl4",
              "name": "DpkgMatcherExactIndirectMatch",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CVE-2026-10536 critical vulnerability for libcurl4 package"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "A use-after-free vulnerability exists in libcurl when an application configures an HTTP/2 stream-dependency tree via `CURLOPT_STREAM_DEPENDS` or `CURLOPT_STREAM_DEPENDS_E`, subsequently invokes `curl_easy_reset()`, and finally terminates the handle with `curl_easy_cleanup()`. During this final cleanup phase, libcurl attempts to access and modify an internal structure that was already freed during the reset operation."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://security-tracker.debian.org/tracker/CVE-2026-10536",
              "help": {
