            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-8927-curl",
              "name": "DpkgMatcherExactDirectMatch",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CVE-2026-8927 critical vulnerability for curl package"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "When reusing a libcurl handle for sequential transfers driven by environment-variable proxy configuration, libcurl fails to clear the proxy authentication state between requests. Specifically, if the initial transfer authenticates against `proxyA` using Digest auth, a subsequent transfer routed through `proxyB` erroneously leaks the `Proxy-Authorization:` header intended solely for `proxyA`."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://security-tracker.debian.org/tracker/CVE-2026-8927",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2026-8927\nSeverity: critical\nPackage: curl\nVersion: 7.88.1-10+deb12u15\nFix Version: \nType: deb\nLocation: /var/lib/dpkg/status\nData Namespace: debian:distro:debian:12\nLink: [CVE-2026-8927](https://security-tracker.debian.org/tracker/CVE-2026-8927)",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2026-8927**\n| Severity | Package | Version | Fix Version | Type | Location | Data Namespace | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| critical  | curl  | 7.88.1-10+deb12u15  |   | deb  | /var/lib/dpkg/status  | debian:distro:debian:12  | [CVE-2026-8927](https://security-tracker.debian.org/tracker/CVE-2026-8927)  |\n"
              },
              "properties": {
                "purls": [
                  "pkg:deb/debian/curl@7.88.1-10%2Bdeb12u15?arch=amd64\u0026distro=debian-12"
                ],
                "security-severity": "9.1"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-8927-libcurl4",
              "name": "DpkgMatcherExactIndirectMatch",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CVE-2026-8927 critical vulnerability for libcurl4 package"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "When reusing a libcurl handle for sequential transfers driven by environment-variable proxy configuration, libcurl fails to clear the proxy authentication state between requests. Specifically, if the initial transfer authenticates against `proxyA` using Digest auth, a subsequent transfer routed through `proxyB` erroneously leaks the `Proxy-Authorization:` header intended solely for `proxyA`."
