            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-8376-perl-base",
              "name": "DpkgMatcherExactIndirectMatch",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CVE-2026-8376 critical vulnerability for perl-base package"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "Perl versions through 5.43.10 have a heap buffer overflow when compiling regular expressions with a repeated fixed string on 32-bit builds.  Perl_study_chunk in regcomp_study.c checked the size of the joined substring buffer in characters rather than bytes. For a quantified fixed substring with a large minimum count, the byte length mincount * l could overflow SSize_t, producing an undersized SvGROW allocation; the subsequent copy writes past the end of the buffer.  A caller that compiles an attacker-controlled regular expression on a 32-bit perl build triggers a heap buffer overflow at compile time."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://security-tracker.debian.org/tracker/CVE-2026-8376",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2026-8376\nSeverity: critical\nPackage: perl-base\nVersion: 5.36.0-7+deb12u3\nFix Version: \nType: deb\nLocation: /var/lib/dpkg/status\nData Namespace: debian:distro:debian:12\nLink: [CVE-2026-8376](https://security-tracker.debian.org/tracker/CVE-2026-8376)",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2026-8376**\n| Severity | Package | Version | Fix Version | Type | Location | Data Namespace | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| critical  | perl-base  | 5.36.0-7+deb12u3  |   | deb  | /var/lib/dpkg/status  | debian:distro:debian:12  | [CVE-2026-8376](https://security-tracker.debian.org/tracker/CVE-2026-8376)  |\n"
              },
              "properties": {
                "purls": [
                  "pkg:deb/debian/perl-base@5.36.0-7%2Bdeb12u3?arch=amd64\u0026distro=debian-12\u0026upstream=perl"
                ],
                "security-severity": "9.8"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-12087-perl-base",
              "name": "DpkgMatcherExactIndirectMatch",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CVE-2026-12087 critical vulnerability for perl-base package"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "Socket versions before 2.041 for Perl have an out-of-bounds heap read.  In Socket.xs, pack_ip_mreq_source() checks the length of its source argument before the argument is read, so the check tests the byte length carried over from the preceding multiaddr argument instead. Both addresses occupy a 4-byte field, so a valid multiaddr lets a source of any length pass the check, and the source is then copied into the 4-byte imr_sourceaddr field with a fixed-size copy. A source shorter than 4 bytes is not rejected, and the copy reads up to 3 bytes past the end of its buffer.  Calling pack_ip_mreq_source() with a source value shorter than 4 bytes copies adjacent heap memory into the returned packed structure."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://security-tracker.debian.org/tracker/CVE-2026-12087",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2026-12087\nSeverity: critical\nPackage: perl-base\nVersion: 5.36.0-7+deb12u3\nFix Version: \nType: deb\nLocation: /var/lib/dpkg/status\nData Namespace: debian:distro:debian:12\nLink: [CVE-2026-12087](https://security-tracker.debian.org/tracker/CVE-2026-12087)",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2026-12087**\n| Severity | Package | Version | Fix Version | Type | Location | Data Namespace | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| critical  | perl-base  | 5.36.0-7+deb12u3  |   | deb  | /var/lib/dpkg/status  | debian:distro:debian:12  | [CVE-2026-12087](https://security-tracker.debian.org/tracker/CVE-2026-12087)  |\n"
              },
              "properties": {
                "purls": [
                  "pkg:deb/debian/perl-base@5.36.0-7%2Bdeb12u3?arch=amd64\u0026distro=debian-12\u0026upstream=perl"
                ],
                "security-severity": "9.1"
              }
