            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-48959-perl-base",
              "name": "DpkgMatcherExactIndirectMatch",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CVE-2026-48959 high vulnerability for perl-base package"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "IO::Uncompress::Unzip versions before 2.220 for Perl allow CPU exhaustion via per-byte read loop in fastForward.  fastForward() compares length $offset (the digit count of the offset, 1 to 19) against the chunk size $c instead of $offset itself, so $c shrinks from 16 KiB to 1-19 bytes per iteration.  Extracting a named entry from an attacker supplied zip via IO::Uncompress::Unzip-\u003enew($zip, Name =\u003e $target) drives a per-byte read loop scaling with the entry's compressed size, up to the non-Zip64 4 GiB cap."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://security-tracker.debian.org/tracker/CVE-2026-48959",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2026-48959\nSeverity: high\nPackage: perl-base\nVersion: 5.36.0-7+deb12u3\nFix Version: \nType: deb\nLocation: /var/lib/dpkg/status\nData Namespace: debian:distro:debian:12\nLink: [CVE-2026-48959](https://security-tracker.debian.org/tracker/CVE-2026-48959)",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2026-48959**\n| Severity | Package | Version | Fix Version | Type | Location | Data Namespace | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| high  | perl-base  | 5.36.0-7+deb12u3  |   | deb  | /var/lib/dpkg/status  | debian:distro:debian:12  | [CVE-2026-48959](https://security-tracker.debian.org/tracker/CVE-2026-48959)  |\n"
              },
              "properties": {
                "purls": [
                  "pkg:deb/debian/perl-base@5.36.0-7%2Bdeb12u3?arch=amd64\u0026distro=debian-12\u0026upstream=perl"
                ],
                "security-severity": "7.5"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-8932-curl",
              "name": "DpkgMatcherExactDirectMatch",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CVE-2026-8932 high vulnerability for curl package"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "libcurl would reuse a previously created connection even when some mTLS config related option had been changed that should have prohibited reuse.  libcurl keeps previously used connections in a connection pool for subsequent transfers to reuse if one of them matches the setup. However, some TLS settings related to client certificates were left out from the configuration match checks, making them match too easily. In particular options related to the private key."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://security-tracker.debian.org/tracker/CVE-2026-8932",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2026-8932\nSeverity: high\nPackage: curl\nVersion: 7.88.1-10+deb12u15\nFix Version: \nType: deb\nLocation: /var/lib/dpkg/status\nData Namespace: debian:distro:debian:12\nLink: [CVE-2026-8932](https://security-tracker.debian.org/tracker/CVE-2026-8932)",
