            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-42767-libssl3",
              "name": "DpkgMatcherExactIndirectMatch",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CVE-2026-42767 medium vulnerability for libssl3 package"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "Issue summary: An attacker-controlled CMP (Certificate Management Protocol) server could trigger a NULL pointer dereference in a CMP client application.  Impact summary: A NULL pointer dereference causes a crash of the application and a Denial of Service.  An attacker controlling a CMP server (or acting as a man-in-the-middle) could craft a CMP response containing a CRMF (Certificate Request Message Format) CertRepMessage with an EncryptedValue structure where the symmAlg field has an algorithm OID but no parameters field. When the OpenSSL CMP client processes this response, the NULL dereference occurs, causing a crash of the CMP client.  Applications that process untrusted CMP/CRMF messages may be affected.  The FIPS modules in 4.0, 3.6, 3.5, 3.4, and 3.0 are not affected by this issue, as the affected code is outside the OpenSSL FIPS module boundary."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://security-tracker.debian.org/tracker/CVE-2026-42767",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2026-42767\nSeverity: medium\nPackage: libssl3\nVersion: 3.0.20-1~deb12u2\nFix Version: \nType: deb\nLocation: /var/lib/dpkg/status\nData Namespace: debian:distro:debian:12\nLink: [CVE-2026-42767](https://security-tracker.debian.org/tracker/CVE-2026-42767)",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2026-42767**\n| Severity | Package | Version | Fix Version | Type | Location | Data Namespace | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| medium  | libssl3  | 3.0.20-1~deb12u2  |   | deb  | /var/lib/dpkg/status  | debian:distro:debian:12  | [CVE-2026-42767](https://security-tracker.debian.org/tracker/CVE-2026-42767)  |\n"
              },
              "properties": {
                "purls": [
                  "pkg:deb/debian/libssl3@3.0.20-1~deb12u2?arch=amd64\u0026distro=debian-12\u0026upstream=openssl"
                ],
                "security-severity": "5.9"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-7017-perl-base",
              "name": "DpkgMatcherExactIndirectMatch",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CVE-2026-7017 high vulnerability for perl-base package"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "HTTP::Tiny versions before 0.095 for Perl forward credential headers to cross-origin redirect targets.  When the server returns a 3xx redirect, `_maybe_redirect` follows the `Location:` header and `_prepare_headers_and_cb` re-merges the caller's `headers` argument into the new request, without checking whether the redirect target shares an origin with the original URL. Caller-supplied `Authorization`, `Cookie` and `Proxy-Authorization` headers are therefore re-sent to whatever host the redirect names, across scheme, host or port boundaries, and including `https` to `http` downgrades that expose them in plaintext on the wire.  The HTTP::Tiny POD note that \"Authorization headers will not be included in a redirected request\" applied only to the URL-userinfo Basic-auth path, not to headers passed explicitly by the caller."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://security-tracker.debian.org/tracker/CVE-2026-7017",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2026-7017\nSeverity: high\nPackage: perl-base\nVersion: 5.36.0-7+deb12u3\nFix Version: \nType: deb\nLocation: /var/lib/dpkg/status\nData Namespace: debian:distro:debian:12\nLink: [CVE-2026-7017](https://security-tracker.debian.org/tracker/CVE-2026-7017)",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2026-7017**\n| Severity | Package | Version | Fix Version | Type | Location | Data Namespace | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| high  | perl-base  | 5.36.0-7+deb12u3  |   | deb  | /var/lib/dpkg/status  | debian:distro:debian:12  | [CVE-2026-7017](https://security-tracker.debian.org/tracker/CVE-2026-7017)  |\n"
              },
              "properties": {
                "purls": [
                  "pkg:deb/debian/perl-base@5.36.0-7%2Bdeb12u3?arch=amd64\u0026distro=debian-12\u0026upstream=perl"
                ],
                "security-severity": "7.1"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-34743-liblzma5",
              "name": "DpkgMatcherExactIndirectMatch",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CVE-2026-34743 medium vulnerability for liblzma5 package"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "XZ Utils provide a general-purpose data-compression library plus command-line tools. Prior to version 5.8.3, if lzma_index_decoder() was used to decode an Index that contained no Records, the resulting lzma_index was left in a state where where a subsequent lzma_index_append() would allocate too little memory, and a buffer overflow would occur. This issue has been patched in version 5.8.3."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://security-tracker.debian.org/tracker/CVE-2026-34743",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2026-34743\nSeverity: medium\nPackage: liblzma5\nVersion: 5.4.1-1+deb12u1\nFix Version: \nType: deb\nLocation: /var/lib/dpkg/status\nData Namespace: debian:distro:debian:12\nLink: [CVE-2026-34743](https://security-tracker.debian.org/tracker/CVE-2026-34743)",
