            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-48961-perl-base",
              "name": "DpkgMatcherExactIndirectMatch",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CVE-2026-48961 low vulnerability for perl-base package"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "IO::Compress versions from 2.207 before 2.220 for Perl ship a zipdetails CLI tool that crashes with undefined subroutine on Info-ZIP Unix Extra Field with 8-byte UID or GID.  When decode_ux() in bin/zipdetails handles an Info-ZIP Unix Extra Field (tag 0x7875) with UID Size or GID Size set to 8, causing zipdetails to decode an 8-byte UID or GID value, it dispatches through decodeLitteEndian(), which calls a misnamed helper unpackValueQ. The actual function defined in the same file is unpackValue_Q (with underscore); the call raises 'Undefined subroutine \u0026main::unpackValueQ' and the script exits with status 255.  Library callers of IO::Compress and IO::Uncompress are not affected; the defect is in the bundled CLI tool."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://security-tracker.debian.org/tracker/CVE-2026-48961",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2026-48961\nSeverity: low\nPackage: perl-base\nVersion: 5.36.0-7+deb12u3\nFix Version: \nType: deb\nLocation: /var/lib/dpkg/status\nData Namespace: debian:distro:debian:12\nLink: [CVE-2026-48961](https://security-tracker.debian.org/tracker/CVE-2026-48961)",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2026-48961**\n| Severity | Package | Version | Fix Version | Type | Location | Data Namespace | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| low  | perl-base  | 5.36.0-7+deb12u3  |   | deb  | /var/lib/dpkg/status  | debian:distro:debian:12  | [CVE-2026-48961](https://security-tracker.debian.org/tracker/CVE-2026-48961)  |\n"
              },
              "properties": {
                "purls": [
                  "pkg:deb/debian/perl-base@5.36.0-7%2Bdeb12u3?arch=amd64\u0026distro=debian-12\u0026upstream=perl"
                ],
                "security-severity": "7.3"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-11850-libgssapi-krb5-2",
              "name": "DpkgMatcherExactIndirectMatch",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CVE-2026-11850 low vulnerability for libgssapi-krb5-2 package"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "An integer underflow vulnerability was found in MIT krb5 in the berval2tl_data() function in plugins/kdb/ldap/libkdb_ldap/ldap_principal2.c. The function performs an unsigned subtraction (bv_len - 2) without a prior bounds check. When bv_len is 0 or 1, the subtraction wraps to a large value which is then truncated to uint16_t, yielding 0xFFFE (65534) or 0xFFFF (65535). The subsequent malloc succeeds and memcpy reads up to 65534 bytes from a 0-1 byte buffer, resulting in a heap out-of-bounds read. The attack vector involves a malicious or compromised LDAP KDB backend returning a krbExtraData attribute with bv_len \u003c 2, triggering the underflow when the KDC or kadmind reads principal data."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://security-tracker.debian.org/tracker/CVE-2026-11850",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2026-11850\nSeverity: low\nPackage: libgssapi-krb5-2\nVersion: 1.20.1-2+deb12u5\nFix Version: \nType: deb\nLocation: /var/lib/dpkg/status\nData Namespace: debian:distro:debian:12\nLink: [CVE-2026-11850](https://security-tracker.debian.org/tracker/CVE-2026-11850)",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2026-11850**\n| Severity | Package | Version | Fix Version | Type | Location | Data Namespace | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| low  | libgssapi-krb5-2  | 1.20.1-2+deb12u5  |   | deb  | /var/lib/dpkg/status  | debian:distro:debian:12  | [CVE-2026-11850](https://security-tracker.debian.org/tracker/CVE-2026-11850)  |\n"
              },
              "properties": {
                "purls": [
                  "pkg:deb/debian/libgssapi-krb5-2@1.20.1-2%2Bdeb12u5?arch=amd64\u0026distro=debian-12\u0026upstream=krb5"
                ],
                "security-severity": "5.0"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-11850-libk5crypto3",
              "name": "DpkgMatcherExactIndirectMatch",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CVE-2026-11850 low vulnerability for libk5crypto3 package"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "An integer underflow vulnerability was found in MIT krb5 in the berval2tl_data() function in plugins/kdb/ldap/libkdb_ldap/ldap_principal2.c. The function performs an unsigned subtraction (bv_len - 2) without a prior bounds check. When bv_len is 0 or 1, the subtraction wraps to a large value which is then truncated to uint16_t, yielding 0xFFFE (65534) or 0xFFFF (65535). The subsequent malloc succeeds and memcpy reads up to 65534 bytes from a 0-1 byte buffer, resulting in a heap out-of-bounds read. The attack vector involves a malicious or compromised LDAP KDB backend returning a krbExtraData attribute with bv_len \u003c 2, triggering the underflow when the KDC or kadmind reads principal data."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://security-tracker.debian.org/tracker/CVE-2026-11850",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2026-11850\nSeverity: low\nPackage: libk5crypto3\nVersion: 1.20.1-2+deb12u5\nFix Version: \nType: deb\nLocation: /var/lib/dpkg/status\nData Namespace: debian:distro:debian:12\nLink: [CVE-2026-11850](https://security-tracker.debian.org/tracker/CVE-2026-11850)",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2026-11850**\n| Severity | Package | Version | Fix Version | Type | Location | Data Namespace | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| low  | libk5crypto3  | 1.20.1-2+deb12u5  |   | deb  | /var/lib/dpkg/status  | debian:distro:debian:12  | [CVE-2026-11850](https://security-tracker.debian.org/tracker/CVE-2026-11850)  |\n"
              },
              "properties": {
                "purls": [
                  "pkg:deb/debian/libk5crypto3@1.20.1-2%2Bdeb12u5?arch=amd64\u0026distro=debian-12\u0026upstream=krb5"
                ],
                "security-severity": "5.0"
              }
